  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_AS_READ",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 1.4,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.2,
    "rationale": "The 18 h aliquot was read at three dilutions, and the dilution-corrected values are about the same as the undiluted reading. The undiluted reading was 1.34. The ×10 reading (two replicates) corrected to 1.47, the ×20 reading (two replicates) to 1.33, and the ×40 reading (one replicate) to 1.40. Only the ×10 value is clearly higher. The ×20 value matches the undiluted reading. The mean of the three, about 1.40, is roughly 4% above 1.34, which is within the scatter between dilutions. If the reader were saturating, the corrected values would rise steadily with dilution, and they do not. The 6 h aliquot, read ×10, corrected to 0.99 against 0.93 undiluted, which is mild, and the reading is not near the plateau. The flat plateau at about 1.35 from 7 h onward therefore looks like real stationary phase and not a hidden increase in biomass. I did not detect a significant undercount. The remaining uncertainty is the ×10 result and the small budget, which left only single replicates at some dilutions."
  },
